The points of inflection of a normal curve are at $x=64$ and $x=88$.
What are the mean and the standard deviation?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.1cm, y=1cm]
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.6:3.6, samples=90, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\fill (-1,1.46) circle (2pt);
\fill (1,1.46) circle (2pt);
\draw[dashed] (-1,0) -- (-1,1.46);
\draw[dashed] (1,0) -- (1,1.46);
\draw (-1,0) -- (-1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$64$};
\draw (1,0) -- (1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$88$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
